<title>LITHUANIA: Lithuanian three-month T-bill rate dips.</title>
<headline>Lithuanian three-month T-bill rate dips.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield at an auction of Lithuanian 98-day Treasury bills was slightly lower at 11.38 percent than the 12.58 average yield at a recent sale of 91-day paper, the central bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>All amounts are in millions of litas.</p>
<p> MATURITY   AV RATE  (LAST TIME)   MIN/MAX   ISSUE   BID    SOLD</p>
<p> 98-day	11.38     12.58	10.0/12.0   40   116.683   40</p>
<p>Settlement date for today's auction is November 22 and the bills mature on February 28.</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
